      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.065,
            0.378,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.119,
            0.344,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.152,
            0.885,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "Evaluate these expressions by thinking of them as the resulting movement of combining button presses: a. (+ 1) + (+ 4) = b. (+ 4) + (+ 1) = c. (+ 4) + (–   3) + (– 2) = d. (– 1) + (+ 2) + (– 3) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.265,
            0.324,
            0.285
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Back to zero!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.291,
            0.754,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "On the ground floor, Basant is in a great hurry and by mistake he presses +3. What can he do to cancel it and stay on the ground floor? He can cancel it by pressing – 3. That is, (+3) + (– 3) = 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.378,
            0.755,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "We call – 3 the inverse of +3. Similarly, the inverse of – 3 is +3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.426,
            0.753,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "If Basant now presses +4 and then presses – 4 in the lift, where will he reach?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.472,
            0.754,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "Here is another way to think of the concept of inverse. If you are at Floor +4 and you press its inverse – 4, then you are back to zero, the ground floor! If you are at Floor – 2 and press its inverse +2, then you go to (– 2) + (+2) = 0, again the ground floor!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.584,
            0.599,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "Write the inverses of these numbers: +4, –4, –3, 0, +2, –1."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.773,
            0.276,
            0.92,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.635,
            0.615,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": "Connect the inverses by drawing lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.659,
            0.619,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.753,
            0.568,
            0.775
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Comparing numbers using floors"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.784,
            0.491,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "Who is on the lowest floor?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.81,
            0.71,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "1. Jay is in the Art Centre. So, he is on Floor +2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.831,
            0.772,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": "2. Asin is in the Sports Centre. So, she is on Floor \\_\\_\\_."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.851,
            0.811,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "3. Binnu is in the Cinema Centre. So, she is on Floor"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.871,
            0.755,
